# The seeds and mulch state files are id-keyed JSONL whose writers REWRITE
# rows in place (closing an issue rewrites its row and every sibling's
# blockedBy; writePlans/writeTemplates rewrite plans and templates; mulch
# upserts merge outcomes into existing records). merge=union therefore
# emitted two contradictory copies of any concurrently rewritten row
# (warren-9c90). merge=seeds-jsonl runs scripts/merge-seeds-jsonl.ts, a real
# 3-way id-keyed merge registered via `git config merge.seeds-jsonl.driver`
# in package.json's prepare script.
# DO NOT let `sd doctor --fix` or `sd init` re-add a `merge=union` line for
# these paths. Both tools GENERATE the union lines and match on the literal
# string, so they report a correct driver as a "missing" entry and APPEND the
# union line back. .gitattributes is LAST MATCH WINS, so an appended union
# line silently OVERRIDES the driver above it and restores the bug while
# doctor calls the repo healthy. `bun run check:merge-strategy` (inside the
# lint gate) asks git what it actually resolves and fails if that happens.
# Upstream fix tracked as seeds-6e2d.
# The .canopy/* merge=union entries were removed: canopy was retired (pl-3a79)
# and those files no longer exist.
.seeds/issues.jsonl merge=seeds-jsonl
.seeds/templates.jsonl merge=seeds-jsonl
.seeds/plans.jsonl merge=seeds-jsonl
.mulch/expertise/*.jsonl merge=seeds-jsonl
